\if{html}{\out{<a id="method-CurrencyOption-initialize"></a>}}
\if{latex}{\out{\hypertarget{method-CurrencyOption-initialize}{}}}
\subsection{\code{CurrencyOption$new()}}{
  Looks the option up in UBI's currency options segment and keeps its details.

An order's quantity is counted in quotation units and must be a whole number of lots.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{CurrencyOption$new(
  exchange,
  underlying_symbol,
  expiry_date,
  strike_price,
  option_type,
  underlying = NULL,
  unified_broker_interface = NULL
)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{exchange}}{The character exchange the option trades on, \code{"nse"} or \code{"bse"}.}
      \item{\code{underlying_symbol}}{The character symbol of the pair the option is written on, such as \code{"USDINR"}.}
      \item{\code{expiry_date}}{The day the option expires, as a \code{Date} or a \code{"YYYY-MM-DD"} character value.}
      \item{\code{strike_price}}{The numeric strike price of the option, quoted in the pair's own rate units.}
      \item{\code{option_type}}{The character option type, \code{"CE"} for a call or \code{"PE"} for a put.}
      \item{\code{underlying}}{The \code{Instrument} the option is written on, such as the \code{CurrencyFutures} it is priced off, which is also what is found when none is given, which the option keeps and uses for \code{underlying} and \code{underlying_price}, or \code{NULL} to use UBI's link to the underlying or else the family's default, looked up on every read.}
      \item{\code{unified_broker_interface}}{The \code{UnifiedBrokerInterface} to send requests through, or \code{NULL} to share one client among all instruments.}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors: signals \code{TypeError} when \code{underlying} is given and is not an \code{Instrument}; \code{CurrencyOptionError} when UBI has no such option, or the instrument it returned is not in the currency options segment; and a \code{UnifiedBrokerInterfaceError} subclass for any other failure reported by, or on the way to, UBI.
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    A new \code{CurrencyOption} object.
  }
}

